  "content": "<p>Check your understanding of this lesson. Your answers aren't recorded.</p>\n<multiple-choice question=\"What is the main benefit of building an environment from a modular kit?\" single-option=\"\" randomize=\"\">\n  <input type=\"checkbox\" value=\"Pieces can be reused and snapped together to build many layouts efficiently\" data-correct=\"true\">\n  <input type=\"checkbox\" value=\"Every piece needs its own unique texture\">\n  <input type=\"checkbox\" value=\"It removes the need for level design\">\n  <input type=\"checkbox\" value=\"It increases draw calls, which improves quality\">\n</multiple-choice>\n<true-false-question question=\"Modular pieces are easier to assemble when they are built to a consistent grid size.\">\n  <input type=\"checkbox\" value=\"True\" data-correct=\"true\">\n  <input type=\"checkbox\" value=\"False\">\n</true-false-question>\n<self-check title=\"Think it through\">\n  <p slot=\"question\">How can lighting and landmarks guide a player through an environment?</p>\n  <p>Brighter or contrasting light and color draw the eye toward the path, framing and leading lines point the way, and distinctive landmarks visible from a distance help players keep their bearings.</p>\n</self-check>\n"
}